#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Anteil"
msgstr "Amount"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Baukasten: Farben"
msgstr "Baukasten: Colors"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Bootstrap (100–900)"
msgstr "Bootstrap (100–900)"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json acf-json/group_zpt_settings_typo_defaults.json
msgid "Eigene"
msgstr "Custom"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid ""
"Eigene Farben: Name (Kleinbuchstaben, Ziffern, Bindestrich, z. B. ecos-blau) und Grundfarbe. Leere Shades werden aus "
"der Grundfarbe berechnet (Vorschau), eingetragene überschreiben die Berechnung. Werte: Hexwert oder HTML-Farbname. "
"Klassen z. B. .bg-ecos-blau-300, CSS-Variablen --theme-ecos-blau-300. Die Shades legt der Tab „Einstellungen“ fest."
msgstr ""
"Custom colors: name (lowercase letters, digits, hyphen, e.g. ecos-blue) and base color. Empty shades are calculated "
"from the base color (preview), entered ones override the calculation. Values: hex value or HTML color name. Classes "
"e.g. .bg-ecos-blue-300, CSS variables --theme-ecos-blue-300. The shades are defined in the “Settings” tab."

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Einstellungen"
msgstr "Settings"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Farbe hinzufügen"
msgstr "Add color"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Farben in WordPress"
msgstr "Colors in WordPress"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Grundfarbe"
msgstr "Base color"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid ""
"Lädt die Shades der Vorlage in die Tabelle, danach anpassbar (wird dann zu „Eigene“). Nach dem Speichern zeigt der "
"Tab „Farbpalette“ die neuen Shades."
msgstr ""
"Loads the preset’s shades into the table, adjustable afterwards (then becomes “Custom”). After saving, the “Color "
"palette” tab shows the new shades."

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Mischen"
msgstr "Mix"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid ""
"Name + Farbe (Palettenfarbe mit Shading oder eigene). Ganze Palettenfarbe → die Systemfarbe übernimmt deren Shades; "
"mit Shading oder eigene Farbe → daraus werden die Shades berechnet. Bootstrap-Namen (primary, secondary, tertiary, "
"quaternary, success, info, warning, danger, light, dark, black, white, gray) setzen auch Bootstraps Farbe (.btn-"
"primary, .text-bg-dark …); nicht angelegte behalten Bootstraps Wert (--theme-primary = --bs-primary). Eigene Namen "
"(z. B. accent oder section für einen Hintergrund) ergeben .text-accent, .bg-section, .bg-section-100, --theme-section "
"…."
msgstr ""
"Name + color (palette color with shading or custom). Whole palette color → the system color takes over its shades; "
"with shading or custom color → the shades are calculated from it. Bootstrap names (primary, secondary, tertiary, "
"quaternary, success, info, warning, danger, light, dark, black, white, gray) also set Bootstrap’s color (.btn-"
"primary, .text-bg-dark …); those not created keep Bootstrap’s value (--theme-primary = --bs-primary). Custom names "
"(e.g. accent or section for a background) result in .text-accent, .bg-section, .bg-section-100, --theme-section …."

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid ""
"Nur diese Farben erscheinen in WordPress: in den Farbauswahlen der Komponenten und Einstellungen (Farbe + Shading) "
"und in der Farbpalette von Block-Editor und klassischem Editor. Reihenfolge = Reihenfolge in der Palette. Leer = alle "
"Farben. Die Systemfarben-Definition zeigt weiter die ganze Palette. Neue Einträge wirken nach dem Speichern."
msgstr ""
"Only these colors appear in WordPress: in the color pickers of components and settings (color + shading) and in the "
"color palette of the block editor and classic editor. Order = order in the palette. Empty = all colors. The system "
"color definition still shows the whole palette. New entries take effect after saving."

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid ""
"Reihenfolge hell → dunkel. Name = Endung der Klassen und Variablen (.bg-primary-300, --theme-primary-light). Genau "
"ein Shade ist die Grundfarbe; die anderen werden aus ihr berechnet: aufhellen = mit Weiß mischen, abdunkeln = mit "
"Schwarz mischen."
msgstr ""
"Order light → dark. Name = suffix of the classes and variables (.bg-primary-300, --theme-primary-light). Exactly one "
"shade is the base color; the others are calculated from it: lighten = mix with white, darken = mix with black."

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Shade hinzufügen"
msgstr "Add shade"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Shades"
msgstr "Shades"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Simple (light, base, dark)"
msgstr "Simple (light, base, dark)"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Systemfarbe hinzufügen"
msgstr "Add system color"

#: acf-json/group_zpt_settings_style.json
msgid "Tailwind (50–950)"
msgstr "Tailwind (50–950)"

